---
import {componentMap as map} from '../../../design-system/studio/component-map.ts';
const methods=[['Owl · Information architecture','Page purpose, customer tasks, taxonomy and navigation','Applied by coordinator; customer research remains a hypothesis'],['Impeccable','Composition and visual direction','Actual context/seed plus selected method in a fresh creator run'],['Taste','Page argument, image roles and whole-page art direction','Actual direction draw plus method/references in a fresh creator run'],['Meng To','Documentary editorial flow and clear offer selection','Fresh creator run; booking omitted because unavailable'],['Emil Kowalski','Purpose, feedback, interruption and reduced motion','Applied to shared controls: press160ms, hover160ms, native navigation'],['Jakub Krehel','Type hierarchy, wrapping, font loading and readable controls','Typography checklist for browser review; no new font chosen by critic']];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>101 · Component and skill map</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;color:#222;background:#f5f4ee;font:16px/1.5 system-ui}main{max-width:1300px;margin:auto;padding:2rem clamp(1rem,4vw,4rem)}h1{font-size:clamp(2.7rem,6vw,5rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.05;max-width:18ch;margin:2.5rem 0}h2{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.2}h3{margin:0;font-size:1.3rem}a{color:inherit}label{display:block;margin:1.5rem 0}select,input{font:inherit;padding:.8rem;max-width:100%}.flow{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;list-style:none;padding:0}.flow li{padding:1rem;background:#dce4d6}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.card{background:white;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid #d4d7ce;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.tag{display:inline-block;font-size:.8rem;padding:.3rem .6rem;background:#e8ece4;margin:.4rem .4rem 0 0}.state{font-weight:600}.card ul{padding-left:1.2rem;font-size:.875rem}.muted{color:#5a6256}.full{max-width:75ch}.methods{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:2rem 0}.method{border-top:1px solid #888;padding-top:1rem}.contract{background:#dce4d6;padding:1.5rem;margin:2rem 0}details{margin-top:1rem}summary{cursor:pointer}a:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #8b2f28;outline-offset:4px}[hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:760px){.cards,.methods{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style></head><body><main><a href="/studio/">Back to Honorato concepts</a><h1>A map of what each piece is for.</h1><p class="full">Skills guide design decisions. Components implement a specific behavior. Runtime libraries execute code. References supply examples. None of those substitutes for a page’s purpose or business evidence.</p><ol class="flow"><li>Customer task</li><li>Page & photo plan</li><li>Skill role</li><li>Component contract</li><li>Render & inspect</li></ol>
<h2>Methods used in this exploration</h2><div class="methods">{methods.map(([name,role,status])=><article class="method"><h3>{name}</h3><p>{role}</p><p class="muted">{status}</p></article>)}</div><p class="full muted">Other named families remain in the <a href="/sources/">full source inventory</a>. This map does not mark them executed. GSAP is an optional runtime/method for a justified timeline; no animation package is required for native menu filtering.</p>
<h2>Choose by the visitor’s task</h2><label>Capability<select id="capability"><option value="all">All capabilities</option>{map.capabilities.map(c=><option value={c.id}>{c.label}</option>)}</select></label><p id="count" role="status">{map.components.length} implementations and sources</p><div class="contract" id="contract"><strong>Contract first</strong><p>Select a task to see required evidence and the honest missing-data fallback.</p></div><div class="cards">{map.components.map(c=><article class="card" data-capabilities={c.capabilities.join(' ')}><h3>{c.name}</h3><p class="state">{c.state.replaceAll('_',' ')}</p><div>{c.capabilities.map(cap=><span class="tag">{cap}</span>)}</div><p>{c.framework}</p><p class="muted">{c.adoption_reason}</p><details><summary>Source, dependencies and license</summary><p>{'source_repository' in c?c.source_repository:c.source_url}</p><p>Revision: {c.revision||'Not pinned; inspect selected item'}</p><ul>{c.paths.map(p=><li>{p}</li>)}</ul><p>{Array.isArray(c.dependency_closure)?c.dependency_closure.join(', '):c.dependency_closure}</p><p>{c.license}</p>{'adapter' in c&&<p>Local adapter: {c.adapter}</p>}</details></article>)}</div><p class="muted">Source paths have been verified for the pinned repositories. Successful integration and complete accessibility validation are separate claims. Each adopted external file still needs its own license and dependency review.</p>
<script define:vars={{capabilities:map.capabilities}}>
const select=document.getElementById('capability');select.addEventListener('change',()=>{let count=0;for(const card of document.querySelectorAll('[data-capabilities]')){card.hidden=select.value!=='all'&&!card.dataset.capabilities.split(' ').includes(select.value);if(!card.hidden)count++}document.getElementById('count').textContent=count+' implementations and sources';const c=capabilities.find(c=>c.id===select.value),box=document.getElementById('contract');box.replaceChildren();const title=document.createElement('strong'),p=document.createElement('p');title.textContent=c?c.label:'Contract first';p.textContent=c?'Needs: '+c.inputs.join(', ')+'. Missing evidence: '+c.fallback+'.':'Select a task to see required evidence and the honest missing-data fallback.';box.append(title,p)});
</script></main></body></html>
